  "method": "Each district's real SMAP grid cells (few per district at 9km) are sampled directly via Earth Engine (ee.Image.sample over the district polygon -- each cell's own value AND location kept, not collapsed into one reduceRegion mean). Village tier: the SMAP cell nearest to the village polygon's centroid (nearest cell-center match). Block tier: mean + standard deviation of its villages' assigned cell values, N = village count. District tier: mean + standard deviation of the real SMAP cells sampled directly over the district polygon, N = cell count (independent of village-boundary coverage). State tier (computed client-side in the dashboard loader): mean + standard deviation of its districts' values, N = districts actually computed so far -- always shown against the state's real total district count.",
  "note": "Resolution is ~9 km -- one SMAP cell covers many villages. Village tier NEVER claims a village-specific value; it always shows the real count of villages sharing that cell. See MERA_KHET_PROMPT.md section B1.",
